{"name":"Sea Breeze","hex":"#a4bfce","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea breeze","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A breeze that blows in the daytime from the sea on to the nearby land.","A cocktail of vodka with cranberry and grapefruit juices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_breeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea Breeze (Bahamas Parliament constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Sea Breeze is a parliamentary constituency represented in the House of Assembly of The Bahamas. It elects one member of parliament (MP) using the first past the post electoral system. It has been represented by Leslia Miller-Brice from the Progressive Liberal Party since 2021."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Bahamas_general_election_2021_-_Results_by_Constituency.svg/330px-Bahamas_general_election_2021_-_Results_by_Constituency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Breeze_(Bahamas_Parliament_constituency)"},{"title":"Sea breeze","blocks":[{"text":"A sea breeze or onshore breeze is a wind that blows in the afternoon from a large body of water toward or onto a landmass. By contrast, a land breeze or offshore breeze is a wind that blows in the night from a landmass toward or onto a large body of water. Sea breezes and land breezes are both important factors in coastal regions' prevailing winds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg/330px-Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_breeze"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg/500px-Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg/1280px-Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg/500px-Sea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea breeze moving across the water (towards the viewer) in Hobart, Tasmania, Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea-breeze_in_Hobart.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/LAKE_BREEZE-en.gif/500px-LAKE_BREEZE-en.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/LAKE_BREEZE-en.gif/500px-LAKE_BREEZE-en.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lake/sea breeze and atmospheric depth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALAKE_BREEZE-en.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Cubanseabreezeconvergence.gif/250px-Cubanseabreezeconvergence.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/99/Cubanseabreezeconvergence.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Cubanseabreezeconvergence.gif/250px-Cubanseabreezeconvergence.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea breeze convergence in Cuba is very similar to that in Florida. The northern sea breeze meets the southern sea breeze, creating a sharp convergence line in the cumulus field.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACubanseabreezeconvergence.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/12_Foot_Skiff_Flat_Out.jpg/500px-12_Foot_Skiff_Flat_Out.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/12_Foot_Skiff_Flat_Out.jpg/500px-12_Foot_Skiff_Flat_Out.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sailing skiff during an afternoon sea breeze in the Sydney Harbour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A12_Foot_Skiff_Flat_Out.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/500px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/1280px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/500px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mediterranean Sea, an enclosed sea flowing into the Atlantic Ocean","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/500px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi